WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.300
Every hotel guest gets the same list of restaurants, the punk rocker and the Bridgerton fan.

2
00:00:05.300 --> 00:00:07.000
Same ten places.

3
00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:13.800
The concierge knows that's wrong. But with 40 arrivals a day, nobody has time to rewrite it for each guest.

4
00:00:13.800 --> 00:00:16.300
So we built Your Kind of Place.

5
00:00:16.300 --> 00:00:21.200
It takes the hotel's own list and edits it for one guest, like an editor with a red pen.

6
00:00:21.200 --> 00:00:23.900
Guest 1 loves Peaky Blinders and Guinness.

7
00:00:23.900 --> 00:00:25.200
Watch the red pen.

8
00:00:25.200 --> 00:00:32.000
Places that don't fit this guest are struck out. Places that do are written in, each with a note in the margin saying why.

9
00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:34.900
The Swan. Dukes Bar. The Orangery.

10
00:00:34.900 --> 00:00:39.600
Every reason comes from Qloo's taste data, not from a language model's imagination.

11
00:00:39.600 --> 00:00:43.700
Same hotel, next guest. Charli XCX and Glossier.

12
00:00:45.600 --> 00:00:48.800
And after dark, the Amy Winehouse fan gets Camden.

13
00:00:48.800 --> 00:00:52.000
Electric Ballroom. The Roundhouse. The Underworld.

14
00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:57.100
Before breakfast, the agent reads tomorrow's arrival notes and has a list ready for every guest.

15
00:00:57.100 --> 00:01:01.000
What it can't handle, like an allergy, it hands back to the concierge.

16
00:01:01.000 --> 00:01:05.900
One tap and it's a message, in the guest's own language, with a map link for every place.

17
00:01:05.900 --> 00:01:08.200
We tested Qloo before we built on it.

18
00:01:08.200 --> 00:01:12.100
A blind AI judge matched 10 of 12 lists to the right guest.

19
00:01:12.100 --> 00:01:16.000
The same question gives the same answer, 99% of the time.

20
00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:20.900
And we tested five more kinds of places. Four failed, so they're not in the product.

21
00:01:20.900 --> 00:01:26.700
And the concierge stays in charge. Accept a line, reject a line. Every edit is their call.

22
00:01:26.700 --> 00:01:32.800
Your guests already told you what they love. Your Kind of Place turns that into the one list they'll actually use.

23
00:01:32.800 --> 00:01:33.600
Try it now.

